                "Having learned the address of Mitchell, Sons, & Candy from a directory at the Berkeley, I was soon at their office in Sackville Street. The gentleman who saw me was particularly suave in manner, but uncommunicative in equal proportion. Having once told me that the Piccadilly house -- which throughout our interview he called a \"mansion\" -- was sold, he considered my business as concluded. \"It is sold, sir,\" was again his laconic reply.",
